note The edges. A call edge leaves level with the line that makes the call when that line is on screen, and from the header otherwise; a callee drawn to the left of its caller gets a short orange curve back instead of a wire across the canvas. Path edges are drawn last, thicker and green, parent step to child step, and carry no label - the node's number is the label.

